{"type":"user","uuid":"f511ef24-9788-4044-9de2-e30d5a525a04","parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T02:02:34.289Z","sessionId":"ff2f30f9-da52-4d33-945e-a5fa2dd95e78","version":"2.1.290","cwd":"<clone>","message":{"role":"user","content":"The usage line doubles the square brackets for optional arguments whose type already puts brackets around its metavar. For example `@click.argument(\"method\", type=click.Choice([\"foo\", \"bar\", \"baz\"]), nargs=-1)` shows `Usage: cli [OPTIONS] [[foo|bar|baz]]...` instead of `[foo|bar|baz]...`, and an optional `click.DateTime(formats=[\"%Y-%m-%d\"])` argument shows `[[%Y-%m-%d]]`. Fix it so these get a single pair of brackets without changing how other arguments are shown, and add a regression test. The existing tests must keep passing."}}
